#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "An introduction to VQE covering basic building blocks and applications."
msgstr ""

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Overview"
msgstr "Ikhtisar"

#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Overview {#overview}"
msgstr "Ikhtisar {#overview}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![\"Hero image\"](/learning/images/courses/quantum-chem-with-vqe/hero.svg)\n"
msgstr "![\"Hero image\"](/learning/images/courses/quantum-chem-with-vqe/hero.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Welcome to **Quantum chemistry with VQE**. The variational quantum eigensolver (VQE) is a quantum algorithm with applications in quantum chemistry and simulation. In this introductory course, you will learn the basic building blocks of VQE, options in its implementation, and a few applications. Content is delivered through a combination of text, video, and code.\n"
msgstr "Selamat datang di **Kimia kuantum dengan VQE**. Variational quantum eigensolver (VQE) adalah algoritma kuantum dengan aplikasi dalam kimia kuantum dan simulasi. Dalam kursus pengantar ini, Anda akan mempelajari blok-blok bangunan dasar VQE, pilihan dalam implementasinya, dan beberapa aplikasi. Konten disampaikan melalui kombinasi teks, video, dan kode.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Principle topics include:\n"
msgstr "Topik-topik utama meliputi:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Hamiltonians\n"
msgstr "Hamiltonian\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Ansaetze\n"
msgstr "Ansaetze\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Classical optimizers\n"
msgstr "Optimizer klasik\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Finding ground state energies using Qiskit patterns\n"
msgstr "Menemukan energi keadaan dasar menggunakan pola Qiskit\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Finding bond lengths using Qiskit patterns\n"
msgstr "Menemukan panjang ikatan menggunakan pola Qiskit\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This course focuses on applications to quantum chemistry, though many of the same building blocks (ansatz circuits, classical optimizers, and the Qiskit patterns framework) can be applied to a wide range of fields outside quantum chemistry.\n"
msgstr "Kursus ini berfokus pada aplikasi kimia kuantum, meskipun banyak blok bangunan yang sama (Circuit ansatz, optimizer klasik, dan kerangka pola Qiskit) dapat diterapkan pada berbagai bidang di luar kimia kuantum.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Helpful resources {#helpful-resources}"
msgstr "Sumber daya berguna {#helpful-resources}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This introduction to VQE is designed for intermediate learners of quantum computing techniques. No background in VQE is required. Familiarity with Qiskit, and some familiarity with quantum mechanics and related mathematics (such as operators) is assumed. We recommend devoting approximately 6-10 hours to completing this content, depending on one's prior experience.\n"
msgstr "Pengantar VQE ini dirancang untuk peserta tingkat menengah dalam teknik komputasi kuantum. Tidak diperlukan latar belakang dalam VQE. Anda dianggap sudah familier dengan Qiskit, serta setidaknya mengenal mekanika kuantum dan matematika terkait (seperti operator). Kami menyarankan untuk meluangkan sekitar 6-10 jam guna menyelesaikan konten ini, tergantung pengalaman Anda sebelumnya.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The course on [Basics of Quantum Information](/learning/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/index) may be helpful in providing background and fundamentals of quantum information and computing.\n"
msgstr "Kursus tentang [Basics of Quantum Information](/learning/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/index) mungkin berguna untuk memberikan latar belakang dan dasar-dasar informasi dan komputasi kuantum.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Exam {#exam}"
msgstr "Ujian {#exam}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To earn your badge for Quantum Chemistry with VQE, take the exam at IBM&reg; Training. This exam is intended to be taken after reading the lessons in this course. After you pass the exam, you will be notified by Credly that you have earned a badge.\n"
msgstr "Untuk mendapatkan lencana Quantum Chemistry with VQE, ikuti ujian di IBM&reg; Training. Ujian ini dimaksudkan untuk diikuti setelah membaca pelajaran-pelajaran dalam kursus ini. Setelah Anda lulus ujian, Anda akan diberitahu oleh Credly bahwa Anda telah mendapatkan lencana.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[Exam](/learning/courses/quantum-chem-with-vqe/exam)\n"
msgstr "[Ujian](/learning/courses/quantum-chem-with-vqe/exam)\n"

